    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py` following the spec. Business days are Monday to Friday and exclude any holiday. For `n > 0` it moves forward and for `n < 0` backward, never counting `start`. For `n == 0` it returns `start` if that is a business day, otherwise the next one. Input validation raises `TypeError` for a `datetime` start, a non-int or `bool` `n`, and any holiday that is not a plain `date`. The holidays iterable is copied into a set up front, so generators work. I wrote 26 pytest cases in `tests/test_solution.py` covering forward and backward moves, the zero case on weekends and holidays, weekend holidays, the accepted holiday container types, and the type errors. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 26.",
